            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "why can't this be std::optional?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Because the boost body parser requires boost::optional, not std::optional.  We could write a function to convert one to another, but that seemed like overkill."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 398,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "on_headers_complete ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 398,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 413,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "BMC_LOG_ERROR ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 413,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Figured this would've been an internal failure that prevents requests, but sure, could also be per request.  Fixed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 427,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "How does this work with the  \"Trailer:\" header?  https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/computer-networks/http-headers-trailer/ ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 427,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't believe it does.  We don't really support trailers in http1 or http2, we certainly don't support sending the content-size in the trailer.  I believe they're only used for chunked encoding, and in that case, you'd have no content-type, so in theory the code would still work, but that's not something I would expect or have tested."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 556,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Do you need a close() here?\nWARNING here since isn't this a 4xx error ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 556,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Switched to warning.\n\nclose() only really needs to be called if we believe the protocol has been violated.  This still closes the connection, it just does it by returning 400 and returning a payload to the user."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 556,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http2_connection.hpp",
                    "line": 558,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "You could check if it is already set.. But HTTP says multiple Content-Lengths are okay if they are the same value :/ \n\nFrom Google:\n```\nHandling Mismatched Values: If a recipient receives multiple Content-Length headers with different values, the message is malformed,\n```\n\n```\n\n    if (req.contentLength)\n    {\n\n       // If new length \n       if \n       {\n            return NGHTTP2_ERR_TEMPORAL_CALLBACK_FAILURE;\n```\n\n\nOh well."
                }
            ],
